I found an inconsistence in jbovlaste:
{tamsmi}, according to official definition, is "x1 has form x2,
similar in form to x3 in property/quality x4".
Although, in notes of {tai} we read "tamsmi is x1 resembles x2 sharing
ideal form/shape x3 in property x4".
Clearly, x2 and x3 switched places. This also affects the definition
of {setai}: "tamsmi modal, 2nd place similarly; resembling ... (in
ideal form).", where according to the official definition of {tamsmi}
it should be "sharing ideal form ... (with something else)" or so.
Am I right?

